Decode-only build of fx2-cmix (https://github.com/kaitz/fx2-cmix), used to measure
how much of the program only the compressor needs. With -DDECODE_ONLY, main() keeps
just the self-extract (no arguments) and -d paths, so --gc-sections drops the
encode-only code (forward transforms, dictionary encoder, arithmetic encoder, etc.).

Apply in an fx2-cmix checkout:  patch -p1 < fx2-cmix-decode-only.patch
Build:  make CFLAGS_DEFINES="-DSEED=923 -DUPDATE_LIMIT=3000 -DDECODE_ONLY" cmix

